    "detailed_description": "<strong>Solve cryptic puzzles, embrace or evade vengeful specters, decide who to trust and unravel a mystery.</strong><br><br>Ancra is a narrative driven, puzzle-horror game. Explore the home of a dying photographer, and solve puzzles to access new areas. <br><br>Encounter strange, conflicting beings and discover a haunting story, piece by piece. Try to understand why you are here, who you are and what role you play in their story.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\"><strong>Features:</strong></h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Classic, survival horror style puzzles.<br><br></li><li> Open level design, multiple routes and supported sequence breaking.<br><br></li><li> Gaining knowledge and information is as important as items and progression.<br><br></li><li> Obtuse objectives and consequences.<br><br></li><li> Unreliable sources of information and conflicting interests of characters.<br><br></li><li> An atmospheric, dynamic environment that alters itself as you progress.<br><br></li><li> Multiple endings, with many small variations.<br><br></li><li> Secret unlockables, such as a Randomiser Mode.<br><br></li><li> A mystery that unravels in layers, and a true story hidden deep within the game.</li></ul><br><i>The photographer's house lies empty, its blood still.<br>Before it stands a figure.<br>The house beckons.<br>Lights within flicker to life. Spirits stir at her return.<br>An Ancra is only complete when it is understood.<br>It requires both Vessel and victim.<br>Whose remains shall you cast to flames?<br>The book of the Serpent shall be your guide.<br>And the final page remains unwritten.</i><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Additional Notes:</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Have a pen and paper on hand, take notes.<br><br></li><li> Save often, perhaps with multiple files.</li></ul>",
